{title: 232 - At the Name of Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #232 • KING'S WESTON • 12.12.11.11}
{lyricist: Caroline M. Noel}
{composer: Ralph Vaughan Williams}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 232}
{meta: tune KING'S WESTON}
{meta: meter 12.12.11.11}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]At the name [F]of [Am/E]Jesus [C]Every [F]knee [Gm]shall [Dm]bow,
[F]Every [Am]tongue confess [F]Him [Dm]King of [Gm]glory now;
[C/E]“Tis the [Gm]Father’s [Am]pleasure [F]We [Gm]should call [C]Him [Bm]Lord,
[Dm]Who [C]from the beginning [Gm]Was the [F]mighty [Dm]Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]At His [F]voice [Am/E]creation [C]sprang [Dm]at once [F]to [Gm]sight,
[F]All the angel [Am]faces, [F]All [Dm]the hosts [Gm]of [F]light,
[C/E]Thrones [Gm]and [C/E]dominations [Gm]stars upon [Bm]their [C]way,
[Dm]All the [C]heavenly orders [Gm]in their [F]great [C/E]array.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Humbled for [F]a [Am/E]season, [C]To [Dm]receive [F]a [Gm]name
[F]From the lips [Am]of sinners, [F]Unto [Dm]whom [Gm]He [F]came;
[C/E]He is [Gm]God [C/E]the [Am]Savior, [F]He [Gm]is Christ [C]the [Bm]Lord,
[Dm]Ever [C/G]to be worshiped, [Gm]Trusted [F]and [C/E]adored.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm]In your [F]hearts [Am/E]enthrone [C]Him: [Dm]There let [F]Him [Gm]subdue
[F]All that is [Am]not holy, [F]All [Dm]that is [Gm]not [F]true;
[C/E]Crown Him [Gm]as [C/E]your [Am]captain [F]in [Gm]temptation's [Bm]hour,
[Dm]Let His [C]will enfold you [Am]in [Gm]its light [F]and [C/E]power.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Dm]Surely, [F]this [Am/E]Lord [Dm]Jesus shall return [Gm]again,
[F]With His Father's [Am]glory, [F]With [Dm]His angel [F]train;
[C/E]For all [Gm]wreaths [C/E]of [Am]empire [F]meet [Gm]upon [C]His [Bm]brow,
[Dm]And [C]our hearts confess [Am]Him [Gm]King of [F]glory [Dm]now.
{end_of_verse}
